WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.822
Rock, paper, scissors.

2
00:00:04.822 --> 00:00:06.656
Rock beats scissors.

3
00:00:06.656 --> 00:00:08.578
Scissors beats paper.

4
00:00:08.578 --> 00:00:10.500
And paper beats rock.

5
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.754
Put the moves in a grid.

6
00:00:12.754 --> 00:00:14.420
A shaded cell means

7
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.483
the row beats the column.

8
00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.229
Nothing beats itself

9
00:00:18.229 --> 00:00:20.530
so the diagonal stays empty.

10
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.013
Now think of taller than.

11
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:25.232
If Ana is taller than Bo

12
00:00:25.232 --> 00:00:27.451
and Bo is taller than Cy

13
00:00:27.451 --> 00:00:29.840
then Ana is taller than Cy.

14
00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.134
Does beats work the same way?

15
00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:35.266
Rock beats scissors

16
00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:37.905
and scissors beats paper.

17
00:00:37.905 --> 00:00:40.443
So does rock beat paper?

18
00:00:40.443 --> 00:00:42.270
Pause and decide.

19
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.104
No.

20
00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:47.628
Paper beats rock

21
00:00:47.628 --> 00:00:51.438
so the cell for rock against paper is empty.

22
00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:53.555
The two steps are there

23
00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:56.010
but the shortcut is missing.

24
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.124
Taller than always has the shortcut.

25
00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:00.353
Beats does not.

26
00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:03.348
That is why the game has no best move.

27
00:01:03.425 --> 00:01:05.575
In this lecture we give that

28
00:01:05.652 --> 00:01:08.800
difference a name, and four more like it.

29
00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.780
So what is a relation?

30
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.053
It is a set of ordered pairs.

31
00:01:15.162 --> 00:01:19.416
We write x R y when the pair with first

32
00:01:19.526 --> 00:01:23.344
entry x and second entry y is in R.

33
00:01:23.453 --> 00:01:26.071
A relation on a set A is

34
00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.580
a subset of A times A.

35
00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:32.968
Take A equal to one, two, three, four

36
00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:36.900
and the relation less than or equal.

37
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.707
Row x, column y.

38
00:01:38.707 --> 00:01:42.745
Row one: one is at most every number.

39
00:01:42.745 --> 00:01:47.315
Row two starts at two, row three at three

40
00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:50.290
and row four has only four.

41
00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.155
Ten pairs in all.

42
00:01:52.155 --> 00:01:55.807
The order matters: two is at most three

43
00:01:55.807 --> 00:01:58.480
but three is not at most two.

44
00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.051
The grid has sixteen cells

45
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.107
and any choice of shaded

46
00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.834
cells is a relation.

47
00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:07.548
So there are two to the sixteen

48
00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.604
sixty-five thousand five

49
00:02:09.687 --> 00:02:11.578
hundred and thirty-six

50
00:02:11.578 --> 00:02:13.470
relations on this set.

51
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.622
Now the properties.

52
00:02:15.705 --> 00:02:18.354
A relation is reflexive if every

53
00:02:18.436 --> 00:02:20.340
x is related to itself.

54
00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.236
On the grid, that is the diagonal.

55
00:02:23.236 --> 00:02:26.795
Less than or equal has the whole diagonal

56
00:02:26.795 --> 00:02:28.450
so it is reflexive.

57
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.541
Irreflexive is the opposite extreme

58
00:02:31.541 --> 00:02:33.597
no x is related to itself.

59
00:02:33.597 --> 00:02:36.490
Picture four bus stops on one street

60
00:02:36.566 --> 00:02:38.698
and relate two stops if they

61
00:02:38.774 --> 00:02:40.525
are next to each other.

62
00:02:40.525 --> 00:02:42.581
No stop is next to itself

63
00:02:42.581 --> 00:02:44.560
so the diagonal is empty.

64
00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.098
Symmetric means: whenever x R y, also y R x.

65
00:02:49.098 --> 00:02:53.145
On the grid, each shaded cell has its mirror

66
00:02:53.235 --> 00:02:55.574
image across the diagonal.

67
00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:58.183
The bus stops are symmetric.

68
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:00.161
Two is next to three

69
00:03:00.161 --> 00:03:02.500
and three is next to two.

70
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.850
Antisymmetric means

71
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:09.350
x R y and y R x together force x equal to y.

72
00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.150
Off the diagonal

73
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.150
no cell and its mirror are both shaded.

74
00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.850
Less than or equal is antisymmetric.

75
00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:22.950
Its shaded cells sit above the diagonal

76
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:26.450
and their mirrors below are empty.

77
00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.385
A warning: these words are not opposites.

78
00:03:30.385 --> 00:03:32.840
Shade only the cell one, one.

79
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.295
Two is not related to itself

80
00:03:35.295 --> 00:03:37.259
so it is not reflexive.

81
00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:40.614
One is, so it is not irreflexive either.

82
00:03:40.614 --> 00:03:41.350
Neither.

83
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.319
Equality, just the diagonal

84
00:03:44.413 --> 00:03:47.219
is symmetric and antisymmetric

85
00:03:47.313 --> 00:03:48.903
at the same time.

86
00:03:48.903 --> 00:03:53.019
And one two, two one, one three is neither

87
00:03:53.019 --> 00:03:55.357
one three has no mirror

88
00:03:55.451 --> 00:03:57.789
while one two and two one

89
00:03:57.883 --> 00:03:59.660
form a mirror pair.

90
00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.272
Transitive means

91
00:04:02.272 --> 00:04:05.620
x R y and y R z give x R z.

92
00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:10.521
Two steps must always have the shortcut.

93
00:04:10.521 --> 00:04:15.781
For less than or equal: one is at most two

94
00:04:15.781 --> 00:04:21.160
two is at most four, so one is at most four.

95
00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.510
The proof works for all integers.

96
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.147
z minus x is z minus y, plus y minus x

97
00:04:28.147 --> 00:04:31.328
two numbers that are not negative

98
00:04:31.328 --> 00:04:34.510
so the sum is not negative either.

99
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.472
The bus stops fail.

100
00:04:36.472 --> 00:04:40.203
One is next to two, and two is next to one

101
00:04:40.203 --> 00:04:42.832
but one is not next to itself.

102
00:04:42.832 --> 00:04:45.377
One counterexample is enough.

103
00:04:45.377 --> 00:04:48.260
Beats broke down in the same way.

104
00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.411
Last, the inverse.

105
00:04:50.498 --> 00:04:53.202
R inverse swaps the two entries

106
00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.947
of every pair in R.

107
00:04:54.947 --> 00:04:56.081
On the grid

108
00:04:56.081 --> 00:04:59.920
it is the mirror image across the diagonal.

109
00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.251
Take less than or equal.

110
00:05:02.251 --> 00:05:05.883
Flip it, and you get greater than or equal

111
00:05:05.883 --> 00:05:09.350
the shaded cells move below the diagonal.

112
00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.896
A relation is symmetric exactly when

113
00:05:12.985 --> 00:05:15.293
it equals its own inverse.

114
00:05:15.293 --> 00:05:17.602
The bus stops: flip them

115
00:05:17.602 --> 00:05:19.466
and nothing changes.

116
00:05:19.466 --> 00:05:22.396
Proving it means two inclusions

117
00:05:22.396 --> 00:05:26.302
R inside R inverse, and R inverse inside R

118
00:05:26.302 --> 00:05:27.900
each by symmetry.

119
00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.525
So read a relation off its grid.

120
00:05:31.525 --> 00:05:35.808
The diagonal tells reflexive or irreflexive.

121
00:05:35.808 --> 00:05:40.090
The mirror tells symmetric or antisymmetric.

122
00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.613
For transitive

123
00:05:41.613 --> 00:05:45.800
check every two-step path for its shortcut.

124
00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.038
One relation has all three of reflexive

125
00:05:50.038 --> 00:05:53.828
symmetric and transitive: same parity.

126
00:05:53.828 --> 00:05:56.549
One and three are both odd

127
00:05:56.549 --> 00:05:59.270
two and four are both even.

128
00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.314
Try it yourself.

129
00:06:01.314 --> 00:06:04.882
Here is a relation on one, two, three.

130
00:06:04.882 --> 00:06:06.254
Draw its grid.

131
00:06:06.254 --> 00:06:09.090
Which properties does it have?

132
00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.153
Same parity behaves like equals.

133
00:06:12.153 --> 00:06:15.290
In part two, relations of that kind

134
00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.241
equivalence relations

135
00:06:17.241 --> 00:06:19.360
sort a set into classes.
